            <div xml:id="d98">

                <pb facs="0240" n="128" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg128"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.01/179: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Davis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-12-02T16:00:00+00:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 2,
                                1919, 4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received December 2, 2:27
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>3481. Your 6209, November 24, 4 p.m. Information received from Foreign Office and
                    outside sources indicates that officially negotiations with Litvinoff have so
                    far been confined entirely to the proposed exchange of prisoners. No reports
                    have been received from British representative regarding a Bolshevik peace
                    offer.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Davis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
